# Files left out of the plugin package: the GitHub release ZIP and WordPress.org SVN trunk.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for what ships. scripts/build-package.sh reads it
# with `rsync --exclude-from=.distignore`, and release.yml hands the resulting folder to the
# 10up deploy action as BUILD_DIR, so the action never applies its own rules.
#
# Syntax is rsync's: a pattern starting with "/" matches only at the plugin root, a pattern
# without "/" matches at any depth (vendor/ included). There is no negation, so never add a
# bare "vendor" or "composer.json" here: vendor/ holds the runtime autoloader and
# libphonenumber, and composer.json must ship next to it (Plugin Check warning
# missing_composer_json_file).

# Hidden files and folders anywhere: .git, .github, .ai, .claude, .wordpress-org (deployed to
# SVN /assets, not into the plugin), .wp-env.json, .phpcs.xml.dist, .releaserc.json,
# .editorconfig, .distignore, .DS_Store, ... Plugin Check reports hidden files as errors.
.*

# Release tooling
/scripts
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/node_modules
/composer.lock
/dist

# Quality tooling and tests
/phpcs.xml
/phpcs.xml.dist
/phpunit.xml
/phpunit.xml.dist
/phpstan.neon
/phpstan.neon.dist
/phpstan-baseline.neon
/playwright.config.ts
/playwright-report
/test-results
/tests
/bin
/wp-cli.local.yml

# AI agent pipeline and contributor documentation
/skills-lock.json
/tasks
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/SDLC.md
/CODE_REVIEW.md
/BACKWARD_COMPATIBILITY.md
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/docs

# Anywhere in the tree, vendor/ included
Thumbs.db
*~
